<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sebastián de Eslava</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1685–1759</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sebastián de Eslava was a Spanish general and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-granada">New Granada</a> from 1740 to 1749. He directed the defence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cartagena-colombia">Cartagena de Indias</a> against the British attack of Admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-vernon">Edward Vernon</a> in 1741, together with the admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blas-de-lezo">Blas de Lezo</a>, and was rewarded with the title Marquis of la Real Defensa. He later served as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>'s secretary of war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sebastian-de-eslava.jpg" alt="Sebastián de Eslava" width="320" height="431" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joaquín Gutiérrez · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Virrey_Sebasti%C3%A1n_de_Eslava.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
